<description>The remote Windows host is missing security update 5060533. It is, therefore, affected by multiple vulnerabilities

  - Heap-based buffer overflow in Windows Routing and Remote Access Service (RRAS) allows an unauthorized     attacker to execute code over a network. (CVE-2025-33066)

  - Improper access control in Windows SMB allows an authorized attacker to elevate privileges over a network.
    (CVE-2025-33073)

  - Use after free in Windows Win32K - GRFX allows an authorized attacker to elevate privileges locally.
    (CVE-2025-32712)

Note that Nessus has not tested for these issues but has instead relied only on the application&apos;s self-reported version number.</description>
