<ReportItem port="0" svc_name="general" protocol="tcp" severity="0" pluginID="44871" pluginName="WMI Windows Feature Enumeration" pluginFamily="Windows">
<cpe>cpe:/o:microsoft:windows</cpe>
<description>Nessus was able to enumerate the server features of the remote host by querying the &apos;Win32_ServerFeature&apos; class of the &apos;\Root\cimv2&apos; WMI namespace for Windows Server versions or the &apos;Win32_OptionalFeature&apos; class of the &apos;\Root\cimv2&apos; WMI namespace for Windows Desktop versions.

Note that Features can only be enumerated for Windows 7 and later for desktop versions.</description>
<fname>wmi_enum_server_features.nbin</fname>
<iavt>0001-T-0754</iavt>
<plugin_modification_date>2025/06/27</plugin_modification_date>
<plugin_name>WMI Windows Feature Enumeration</plugin_name>
<plugin_publication_date>2010/02/24</plugin_publication_date>
<plugin_type>local</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>None</risk_factor>
<script_version>1.251</script_version>
<see_also>https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/cc280268
https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/desktop/WmiSdk/querying-the-status-of-optional-features</see_also>
<solution>n/a</solution>
<synopsis>It is possible to enumerate Windows features using WMI.</synopsis>
<xref>IAVT:0001-T-0754</xref>
<plugin_output>
Nessus enumerated the following Windows features :

  - MSRDC-Infrastructure
